WEBVTT

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.870
<i>In the late 13th century,</i>

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.520
<i>a single nation ravaged and took 
control over most of Eurasia.</i>

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:16.080
<i>It was the Mongol Empire.</i>

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:22.590
<i>Centuries later, researchers who studied 
the prophecies of Nostradamus would say</i>

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.850
<i>that Mongolia was Angolmois,</i>

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.420
<i>the place from which the king 
who destroys the world will be born.</i>

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.000
<i>And that deadly peril is now descending</i>

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.750
<i>on the furthest point of the 
land of the rising sun, Tsushima.</i>

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:51.580
I told you that the Kuchii household 
has no need for a persimmon tree.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.860
This tree is my friend!

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:59.360
Father, I'll do the best 
I can to protect it!

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.250
I won't lose anyone else!

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:06.300
<i>Sheesh... I wish she hadn't 
made me remember that.</i>

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.300
Is Kuchii Jinzaburou here?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.980
I have a message from Princess Teruhi.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:15.720
You are to participate in the strategy 
conference held at the lord's mansion.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.170
Strategy conference?

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:57.140
I am heir to the line of Taira no 
Tomomori, child of Sou Shigehisa,

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:00.880
Sou Sukekuni!

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.150
I fired my arrow at exactly 
the right moment,

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.870
and sent it right through 
the throat of the enemy general.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:12.840
The lord of the Shouni Clan, 
who was watching from the camp,

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.640
stood up and began to cheer.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.630
<b>Lord of Tsushima 
Sou Sukekuni</b>

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:20.220
When I heard the Mongol 
hordes were on their way,

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.970
the excitement I felt that day 
came racing back to me.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:27.850
Now, everyone, take a look 
at this picture scroll.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.360
<i>This is a strategy conference?</i>

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:35.240
<i>It feels more like a meeting 
for a village festival.</i>

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.490
You there, exile.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:42.360
I've heard that the people of Kamakura 
spend all their time playing kemari ball.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.430
It must be rare for you 
to hear stories like these.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.130
Yes.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.800
By the way, my lord.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.410
<b>Adopted Son of the Sou Clan 
Abiru Yajirou</b>

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.420
Who is that exile?

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.680
Don't you think it's bad luck 
to have someone wearing those

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.160
persimmon-colored prisoners' clothes 
during a sacred strategy meeting?

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.880
Abiru Yajirou-dono,

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.760
I asked Father to bring him here.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:07.020
This is Kuchii Jinzaburou, who says he 
wishes to fight on behalf of the Sou Clan.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.380
<i>I did not.</i>

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:09.970
I see.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.280
Come, Princess Teruhi.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:14.310
It's bad manners to just stand there.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.640
Sit.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.150
I'm sorry, Father.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.830
<i>He calls his own daughter "Princess"?</i>

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.830
Now, on to matters of war.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:31.300
The Mongol navy left Gappo Bay 
in Goryeo two days ago,

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.250
but there's been no sign of them.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.360
It seems we've nothing to fear.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.880
<b>Hakata</b>

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.880
<b>Iki</b>

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.880
<b>Tsushima</b>

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.880
<b>Goryeo</b>

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.880
The Mongols will pass by Tsushima.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:45.750
That's correct, my heir?

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:46.470
Yes.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.710
Yes. The Mongol army contains many 
soldiers from my homeland of Goryeo.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:53.140
<b>Oldest Son of the Sou Clan  
Sou Umajirou</b>

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:53.010
According to someone I know 
in the government there,

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:56.490
they say they'd never attack 
their ancient ally Tsushima.

00:04:56.490 --> 00:05:01.370
The Mukuri's huge ships are easily 
capable of going straight to Hakata.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:02.400
<b>Servant of Sou Clan Genpachi</b>

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.380
Tsushima has always been 
a home for strong warriors.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.110
Perhaps they know that.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:07.830
That's ridiculous.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.370
These aren't lowly pirates.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:13.990
The army of an entire empire won't 
just pass right by an enemy base.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:16.710
An army is like the head of a snake.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:22.290
It can only go forward if huge amounts of food 
and manpower can pass through its backbone.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:25.710
And Tsushima is the Mongol army's backbone.

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:26.960
Silence, exile!

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.250
You know nothing of the Mongols
or of Goryeo. What do you know?

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:33.680
Nothing. Except whether 
we're going to win or lose.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:39.800
Now that an army's on the march, 
your ancient alliances mean nothing.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.720
You, old man.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:46.870
Your roof is on fire. How long are you 
going to keep sleeping in your bed?

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:53.450
Everyone, throw him out.

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:59.920
Let us continue the conference, my lord.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.700
<i>Well, I got a little too angry.</i>

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:13.630
<i>I guess even now, 
I still think I'm a samurai.</i>

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:29.880
You idiot!

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:32.050
Don't just sit in the middle of the road.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:33.240
Sorry.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.420
Damn it!

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:37.490
I got up when it was still dark 
to bring these all the way here...

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:39.030
When it was still dark?

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.390
<i>Is this island bigger than I think it is?</i>

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:43.890
Hey, can you tell me something?

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:49.960
Let's say this circle is Tsushima, 
and this spot is its capital.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:52.100
Where's your village, kid?

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.690
That's not what Tsushima looks like.

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:55.980
What do you mean?

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.530
You don't know a thing, do you, outsider?

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:00.890
There's a big inlet on the island

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:04.430
which separates it into two parts: 
the upper and lower province.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:06.930
So it's like this?

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:10.820
Oh, Tsushima is longer and thinner.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:13.640
Then... like this?

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:16.230
Not like that. Further up.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:18.280
Okay, is that it?

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.700
So this is what it looks like, huh?

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:23.780
I grew up on this island, but it's like 
I'm seeing it for the first time.

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:26.470
You have quite the handsome face...

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.450
<i>Five days on foot from north to south,</i>

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:31.760
<i>a day to cross the mountains 
from east to west.</i>

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:34.100
<i>And there's a surprisingly 
large amount of villages.</i>

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.080
<i>It's more like a whole 
country than an island.</i>

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:43.480
Where do we run once the Mukuri come?

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:47.060
I'll be fighting for my clan again.

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:49.210
Where do we get the ships?

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:50.660
Dad's still too sick to stand...

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:54.360
We need to plant next year's 
wheat crop before we can hide...

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:55.500
I guess the marriage is off...

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:00.970
Fascinating.

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:02.890
Get this map down on paper.

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:03.630
Yes, sir.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:07.340
It's been a long time, 
Kuchii Jinzaburou-dono.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:09.490
You're...

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:15.770
It's been two years since we met 
on Komachi Street in Kamakura, huh?

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.820
What do you want with a mere exile?

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:22.160
How cold.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:25.870
We once both served 
the Kamakura, did we not?

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:28.870
We weren't exactly friends.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:31.080
And your clan was far 
more powerful than mine.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:33.080
You're the High General now,

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:37.170
commanding the shogunate's armies 
in Kyushu, are you not?

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:38.940
Shouni Kagesuke-dono.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.870
<b>Shogunate High General  
Shouni Kagesuke</b>

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:44.360
What brings you out here, 
to the ends of the Earth?

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:47.990
Part of it was to learn what 
I could about the Mongols,

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:49.510
but that's not all.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:54.040
Once I got here, I made a decision.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:57.060
I'm providing reinforcements.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.600
I'm sending 3,000 soldiers to Tsushima.

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:05.890
You'll see them arrive in seven days.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:10.630
I'll return to Hakata in a day,

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:12.890
then spend five days readying an army.

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:16.100
And it will take one more 
day for them to appear.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.660
Seven days in all.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:20.770
Well, Kuchii-dono,

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:24.220
can you hold this place until I return?

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:28.680
I'm asking because I know 
your reputation as a warrior.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.290
No, I don't have a reputation...

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:33.450
This was a favorite blade 
of Minamoto-no-Yoshitsune.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:36.850
A century ago, the first founder 
of my clan was given it.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:38.740
Lord Yoshitsune?

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:42.150
It belongs in the hands of a master 
of the Gikei style, like you.

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:43.430
Take it.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.530
Please. Just seven days.

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:50.450
You never were the sort of man 
who should fight at another's behest.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:10:01.370
Get those troops in Hakata 
ready in four days, not five.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.500
It will take one day to get back to Hakata,

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:08.370
but when you head back here, a fleet loaded 
with troops will take two days to get here.

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:11.910
I still need you back here 
in seven days, though. Got it?

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:13.750
Understood.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.860
Where are you going?

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:20.420
Don't tell me you're 
now scared of the Mongols,

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:22.550
and plan to flee on this monk's ship?

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.930
Of course, that's my plan.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:25.600
What?

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:29.140
No, he's simply here to see me off.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.410
Don't worry, princess.

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:33.680
I won't take Kuchii-dono from you.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:38.440
Farewell, Kuchii-dono, and good luck.

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:47.460
He's a little different than I remember him.

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:50.780
Perhaps being in Kamakura 
was too stifling for him.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:53.170
<i>I wish I'd never heard that.</i>

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:55.980
<i>Reinforcements in seven days?</i>

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:59.040
<i>Now I have to count on something 
I know I can't count on.</i>

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:02.150
<i>There's no telling how 
much we'll need this man.</i>

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:04.810
<i>I have to convince him 
to stay here no matter what.</i>

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:11.250
<i>This isn't something I'm good at, but...</i>

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.720
K-Kuchii Jinzaburou-dono?

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:17.270
Dono?

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:25.200
J-Jinzaburou-dono...

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:31.130
I'm actually so afraid, 
I think my heart might burst.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:35.250
Jinzaburou-dono, please...

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:39.430
Will you stay with me forever?

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:44.100
Fine. I'll stay.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:44.950
R-Really?

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:48.350
W-Well, I can't turn down 
a request from a princess.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.720
<i>Too easy.</i>

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:53.820
<i>In the end, he's just an eastern barbarian.</i>

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.420
Father!

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:23.030
We just got word.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:26.120
The Mongol navy has landed in Sasu Bay.

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:28.250
I see.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:31.350
We didn't expect Sasu Bay.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.580
Father, this is a serious matter...

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:35.240
I know.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:49.690
What's that bell?

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:58.470
The Mongols are here?

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:05.430
<i>At twilight, word came that the Mongol 
Fleet had appeared in Sasu Bay.</i>

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:08.840
<i>October 5th. The 11th
year of the Bunmei era...</i>

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:10.690
<i>It was late fall.</i>

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:14.530
Seven days, huh?

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:19.900
We can't use the temple.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.940
The mountain! Head to the mountain!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.820
I can't walk anymore...

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.620
You're in the way, old man.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:29.230
Shut up, brat.

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:34.360
So, Kuchii-dono, will you believe 
this Shouni Kagesuke and join the war?

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:37.180
I don't know. It was just words.

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:40.560
What?

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:42.610
I didn't say anything.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:44.550
Make way!

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.060
The lord is passing through!

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:50.350
My lord, will the Mongols make it 
all the way to the capital here?

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:51.480
Be silent.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:53.470
We don't know that there'll be war.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.220
They may simply have stopped to resupply.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:57.640
<i>There's 300 of them at best, huh?</i>

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:00.310
<i>I'm told the Mongols swarm 
their foes with a huge army...</i>

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:01.590
Father!

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:03.490
Princess Teruhi?

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:06.260
Teruhi! Why are you dressed like that?

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:08.230
Let me join your army.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:11.240
I want to do anything I can 
as a member of the Sou Clan...

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:19.740
You're 17 years old, 
and you still don't know better?

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:21.910
Remember your place.

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:25.260
You haven't forgotten 
your bloodline, have you?

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:29.510
<i>Bloodline? She's not part of the Sou Clan?</i>

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:33.330
I don't care about my bloodline!

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:37.560
I'm part of the Sou Clan, 
the daughter of the Lord of Tsushima,

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:39.650
the daughter of Sou Sukekuni!

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.520
That's who I want to be!

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:44.370
Of course.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:46.630
You're my daughter, Teruhi.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:50.940
The older you are when you have 
children, the more you love them.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.420
Don't worry, Teruhi.

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:56.420
We'll destroy the Mukuri easily.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.930
Gontarou, keep Teruhi here.

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:02.930
Y-Yes, sir.

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:06.910
Everyone, we'll be crossing 
the mountains all night.

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:09.580
The mountains are tougher than the Mukuri!

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:11.300
Be ready!

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:12.180
Yes, sir!

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.970
Father! Brother!

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:16.550
Stay here and wait for good news, Teruhi!

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:17.820
We'll be back!

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:19.730
Take care, Princess!

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:23.870
Everyone...

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:26.960
Kuchii-dono...

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:30.480
It's not hard to guess what's on his mind.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:57.550
<i>The smell...</i>

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:01.050
<i>I've never smelled anything like it.</i>

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:05.140
<i>And this rumbling of strange sounds 
that I've never heard before...</i>

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:12.120
We finally meet.

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:16.850
You're kidding me.

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:18.870
Hold these guys off for seven days?

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.690
We've sighted the enemy vanguard!

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:25.870
Those flags...

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:27.260
Goryeo!

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:30.990
The enemy is at the base of Mt. Ookuma.

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:34.720
The plains in front shall be 
a fine spot for the battle.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:36.010
I see.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:39.260
That's a good spot, 
considering you're on horseback.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:42.330
But they have over 1,000 men.

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:46.850
It'll be a rough fight.

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:50.270
If you like, I'll help you.

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:52.860
What are you doing here?

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.770
Impudent young man...

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:58.500
What can you do on your own?

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:02.410
Our clan fights as one!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.940
We don't want your help, outsider.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:13.040
Kuchii Jinzaburou, 
you shamed me at that meeting,

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:15.590
and I felt great anger.

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:19.040
I told myself I should have killed you.

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:24.150
I was so angry that crossing the mountains 
all night didn't bother me at all.

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:28.780
But you made me realize something.

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:32.740
I was satisfied with the fact 
that I'd fought in the past

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:35.680
and forgot that there was 
more fighting to do.

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:39.140
I order you to head toward the rear.

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:41.040
Guard Teruhi.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.720
Huh? The rear?

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:46.950
I will give you that armor in exchange.

00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:48.080
Lord!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:51.220
That armor belonged to the founder 
of our clan, Taira-no-Tomomori...

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:53.940
It's a relic from a century ago.

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:56.270
I've never been one 
to keep up with the times.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:01.140
I kept this as a good luck charm,

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:03.720
but this picture scroll of that battle

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:06.780
is nothing but a shadow of past glory!

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:09.830
This will be the greatest 
battle of our lives!

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:13.770
Let's give them something 
to put on a nice, big scroll!

00:18:24.760 --> 00:18:28.750
I am...

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:35.830
Descendant of Taira-no-Tomomori, 
who showed his valor in the Genpei War!

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:42.120
Sou Umanojou Sukekuni!

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.520
<i>They all fire their arrows 
at the sound of the signal.</i>

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:58.480
<i>So that's the Mongol's strategy?</i>

00:18:58.480 --> 00:18:59.690
<i>It's genius.</i>

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:02.550
<i>They don't aim at specific targets.</i>

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:04.750
<i>They just shoot them 
up into the air like a net.</i>

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:08.850
<i>Each individual arrow is weaker, 
but there's no need for advanced training,</i>

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:10.590
<i>and each soldier contributes equally.</i>

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:15.670
<i>If they're using a tactic like this, it means 
their soldiers came from different places.</i>

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.050
Bring the spare horses!

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:19.400
Stay strong!

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:20.520
Get closer!

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:23.590
Two hundred steps to the enemy!

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:25.690
One hundred and fifty steps!

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:27.720
One hundred steps!

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:29.230
Attack!

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:43.840
<i>One of their high generals was struck</i>

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:47.270
<i>in the right breast by Sou Umajirou 
and fell from his horse.</i>

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:51.990
<i>Several dozen fell after being shot 
by Sou Sukekuni and Yajirou.</i>

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.860
<i>In later years, the people 
who lived in this land</i>

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:58.350
<i>would speak of Sou Sukekuni's 
deeds on this day</i>

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:01.000
<i>and call him the War God of Sasu.</i>

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:02.630
<i>Well done.</i>

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:03.930
<i>The enemy's ranks are broken.</i>

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:04.850
<i>But...</i>

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:07.270
Father, we're almost to the bay.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.930
Push them into the sea!

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:09.610
Right!

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:13.110
<i>Their huge army is only at a disadvantage 
when it's in that valley.</i>

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:18.270
<i>Are they trying a little too hard 
because it's their own home?</i>

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:25.820
Father, is this...

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:28.380
Why would they do such a thing?

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:49.570
My lord, what is this?

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:51.240
My lord?

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:53.770
My ears...

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:55.640
Yajirou, sound the retreat.

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:56.490
We're leaving.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:57.010
Right!

00:20:57.010 --> 00:20:57.940
Get back to the valley!

00:20:57.940 --> 00:20:59.520
Hurry! Run!

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:02.290
Fall back! Fall back!

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:06.350
More of them? They landed so many?

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.380
Father, hurry!

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:13.390
Umajirou?!

00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:21.500
Damn you!

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:35.480
Very well. I've fought all I need to!

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:09.970
<b>Episode 2:
The War God of Sasu</b>
